      'Greet by the time of day: **buenos días** in the morning, **buenas tardes** from noon until dark, and **buenas noches** in the evening and at night. The ending matches the noun: días is masculine plural (buenos), tardes and noches are feminine plural (buenas). **¿Cómo estás?** is the casual “How are you?”, and you can answer **Muy bien** (very well): **muy** means “very” and **y** means “and”. Put **señor** (Mr., sir) or **señora** (Mrs., ma’am) before a name. Questions and exclamations open with **¿** and **¡**.',
